<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Kummuh</h1><p class="st-meta">1100 BCE – 708 BCE (approx.) · capital Samosata</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Kummuh, a Neo-Hittite kingdom on the upper Euphrates around Samosata, forerunner of later Commagene.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Kummuh arose after the Hittite collapse c. 1180 BCE in the land on the right bank of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samosata">Samosata</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samsat">Samsat</a>. Assyrian texts mention it from the time of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiglath-pileser-i">Tiglath-Pileser I</a>, c. 1100 BCE, when it was a target of raids.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Its kings ruled a farming land of river valleys and wrote inscriptions in Luwian hieroglyphs. Placed between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/assyrian-empire">Assyrian Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-urartu">Kingdom of Urartu</a>, they usually paid tribute to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>; Kushtashpi joined an Urartian alliance against Tiglath-Pileser III and then submitted again.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 708 BCE <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sargon-ii">Sargon II</a> deposed King Muwatalli for conspiring with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-urartu">Urartu</a>, deported its people and made Kummuh an Assyrian province. The name survived as <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-commagene">Commagene</a>, later the Kingdom of Commagene.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kummuh.jpg" alt="Kummuh" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Hans van Deukeren · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NeoHittiteStates.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1100 BCE – 708 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century-bce">12th century BCE</a> – <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Samosata</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Kushtashpi, Muwatalli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Luwian religion</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Luwian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kummukh</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=-904&amp;focus=kummuh" aria-label="Kummuh on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5642 827 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kummuh lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5962 1083L6092 1134"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6092 1134h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5962 1083h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5962 1083h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=-904&amp;focus=kummuh">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

